  "body": "Operators can now discover their durable command history after local cache loss and reconcile a lost submission response using the original command. History pages preserve selected subjects and refuse stale or conflicting reads.\n\nBrowser submission freezes the request bytes before POST, derives the Kernel-compatible BLAKE3 command ID and framed payload digest, and checks every response against that subject. Exact retries accept the original command's current phase, including settled results. The pre-POST journal stores a validated snapshot; serialization hooks, changed caller objects and inconsistent saved subjects cannot replace it. Reload restores saved account/model fields without automatically submitting, and authentication failures retain the journal for reconciliation.\n\nValidation on 4cd0fc89fa44e6f8b1f4c475f63519d9a8ff454c: full local required passed with 245 distinct unit tests and 14 mocked browser tests, typed build, lint, security and docs. Both current [push](https://github.com/neverhuman/bullet-portal/actions/runs/34433938798) and [PR](https://github.com/neverhuman/bullet-portal/actions/runs/34433940212) runs passed all six required jobs. Literal Rust-generated vectors verify browser digest compatibility. Independent static review covered each source packet and the actual test identity delta; no unrelated test was removed or check suppressed.\n\nThese are component proofs. Task-shaped server allocation, native controls, independent completion, persistent installation and authenticated provider recordings remain open. Operating HOLD remains effective.\n",
